  "Id": 142,
  "Title": "AKU alumnus joins IED as the new Director",
  "NewsSubTitle": null,
  "NewsSummary": "Dr Sarfaroz Niyozov, a graduate of the first batch of IED's MEd programme, appointed as Director, IED Pakistan.",
  "GlobalNews": false,
  "AlternateNewsTitle": null,
  "AlternateNewsSubtitle": null,
  "AlternateNewsSummary": null,
  "NewsContent": "<div class=\"ExternalClassA444561C692744CD9DE43851F0CFE761\"><p></p><div>AKU Alumnus, Dr Sarfaroz Niyozov, joins the Institute for Educational Development, Pakistan as the new Director.</div><div><br></div><div>Sarfaroz is a graduate of the first batch of IED's Master of Education (MEd) Programme which he completed with distinction in 1995.&#160;</div><div><br></div><div>Born in Tajikistan, he studied and worked in Tajikistan, Syria, Yemen and Tunisia and also taught at Dushanbe and Khorog universities in Tajikistan before joining IED as an MEd student in 1993.</div><div><br></div><div>The Aga Khan Foundation awarded a scholarship to Sarfaroz to pursue his PhD in Education at the University of Toronto, Canada which he completed in 2001. His PhD research received the best dissertation awards from the Comparative and International Education Society and the American Education Research Association.</div><div><br></div><div>In 2005, Sarfaroz joined the Ontario Institute for Studies in Education (OISE), University of Toronto. He served as an Associate Professor, Curriculum, Teaching and Learning at OISE. Before joining IED, he was serving as Co-Director of the Comparative, International and Development Education Centre and as an editor of the Journal of Curriculum Inquiry at OISE, University of Toronto.</div></div>",
